\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
For every $n\geq 4$, is the codimension-two Urysohn width of all connected complete smooth boundaryless n-manifolds with $Scal\geq 1$ bounded by one constant depending on n only? Urysohn width means the infimum of maximal fiber diameter over continuous maps to simplicial complexes of dimension $\leq n-2$.

\subsection{Short English statement}
For every $n\geq 4$, is the codimension-two Urysohn width of all connected complete smooth boundaryless n-manifolds with $Scal\geq 1$ bounded by one constant depending on n only? Urysohn width means the infimum of maximal fiber diameter over continuous maps to simplicial complexes of dimension $\leq n-2$.

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] Original question source or mathematical context.
\url{https://www.ihes.fr/~gromov/wp-content/uploads/2018/08/101-problemsOct1-2017.pdf}.
\item[S2] OpenAI, manuscript citation page. Source of the formulation motivating this local problem.
\url{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/Positive-scalar-curvature-and-uniform-codimension-two-width-September-23-2026/README.md}.
\end{itemize}

